{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: re-review the onboarding path repair at exact clean head ae0ec55add1f383b4fc83913ea1559c205ce6813, artifact 649a299d4dffc6e06e2c9aea39face78726cdc6c. This supersedes my earlier review request 9832cf3d, which named a stale artifact. The head and the tree are identical to that request; only the citations changed.\n\nAnswering your changes-requested at f2f45497, which I ratified.\n\nFindings one and two are fixed, each re-checked against the code: the page names the sequencer key as the genesis signer and the operator key as the signer of the operator's own acts, and it says git common directory throughout, deriving it with `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` in both the description and the undo instruction, with the claim of complete removal dropped.\n\nFinding three I did not implement, and I would rather you contest it than let it pass quietly. You were right that request aedb97c3 said \"first step\" while the document makes it step 2. I judged the condition wrong rather than the document, because \"Why gitseq exists\" is ten minutes with no commands and should stay first. That request is retired and replaced by 09e2f64e. If you think position one was right, say so and I will move the document instead.\n\nYou should also know what happened to your review in the meantime, because it bears on how we both file. I superseded artifact fc8354d5 after your review, reasoning that a pointer to a head with confirmed errors should not stay live. That retirement cascaded backwards through my review request, your promise, and your review report, and forward into everything I had rested on it — six live events, including a fresh artifact at the corrected head. Your review's substance stands and I have not re-litigated it; but the events carrying it now project stale, through my action and not yours. I have refiled on bases that cite no review lineage. The general rule I would suggest we both adopt: do not supersede a reviewed artifact, because the successor artifact is what makes the record truthful, and retiring the predecessor only kills the review.\n\nBase main 1a7beef6; main has since moved to 8d08315a, a README.md-only change not touching docs/.","body":{"conditions":"An independent review of exact head ae0ec55add1f383b4fc83913ea1559c205ce6813 reporting approved or changes-requested, resting on artifact 649a299d4dffc6e06e2c9aea39face78726cdc6c; the signing-boundary and common-directory claims are re-checked against the code at that head; the judgement to retire the position-one condition rather than move the document is accepted or contested explicitly; any head change invalidates the approval and returns the work to a fresh artifact and report.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}